{"version":"2026.10.11-r25","id":"Q2345425","formula":"H₃⁺","hill":"H3","elements":["H"],"composition":{"H":3.0},"names":{"en":"Trihydrogen cation","ru":"Катион тригидрогена"},"descriptions":{"en":"The trihydrogen cation or protonated molecular hydrogen (IUPAC name: hydrogenonium ion) is a cation (positive ion) with formula H+3, consisting of three hydrogen nuclei (protons) sharing two electrons. The trihydrogen cation is one of the most abundant ions in the universe. It is stable in the interstellar medium (ISM) due to the low temperature and low density of interstellar space.","ru":"Трёхатомный ион водорода (название ИЮПАК[уточнить]: hydrogenonium ion) — катион (положительный молекулярный ион водорода) с формулой H 3 + {\\displaystyle {\\ce {H3^+}}} , состоящий из трёх атомов водорода, разделяющих между собой два электрона. Один из самых распространённых ионов во Вселенной. В условиях сверхмалой плотности межзвёздного пространства и низкой температуры стабилен."},"fame":21,"pubchemCid":null,"mass":null,"charge":1,"smiles":"[HH2+]","inchikey":null,"iupac":null,"classes":[{"qid":"Q113145171","names":{"en":"type of chemical entity","ru":"тип химического объекта","uk":"тип хімічної сутності"}}],"structureInfo":{"kind":"molecule","source":"rdkit","ref":null,"atoms":3,"license":"Computed with RDKit from SMILES (PubChem, Wikidata)"},"structure":{"kind":"molecule","atoms":[{"x":0.0,"y":0.0,"z":0.0,"el":"H"},{"x":-0.708,"y":0.0,"z":0.0,"el":"H"},{"x":0.708,"y":0.0,"z":0.0,"el":"H"}],"bonds":[[0,1,1.0],[0,2,1.0]]},"sources":[{"role":"identity","name":"Wikidata","url":"https://www.wikidata.org/wiki/Q2345425","license":"CC0 1.0"},{"role":"description","name":"Wikipedia (en)","url":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Trihydrogen_cation","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"role":"description","name":"Wikipedia (ru)","url":"https://ru.wikipedia.org/wiki/%D0%A2%D1%80%D1%91%D1%85%D0%B0%D1%82%D0%BE%D0%BC%D0%BD%D1%8B%D0%B9_%D0%B8%D0%BE%D0%BD_%D0%B2%D0%BE%D0%B4%D0%BE%D1%80%D0%BE%D0%B4%D0%B0","lic